{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs","id":890951,"title":"Severed Limbs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-14T20:36:13-07:00","id":890951,"title":"Severed Limbs?","content":"What happens when a wolf loses an arm? Can you regenerate it later? Can you pick it up and heal it back on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:41:54-07:00","id":890953,"title":"","content":"Limbs can grow back, I imagine it similar to Deadpool's hand. But more painful, since regeneration hurts. So if they had some time and skill, as well as the necessary pieces, a werewolf would probably sew it back on and as a Storyteller I'd rule that it would take less time to heal.<br /> <br /> On second thought after re-reading the section it probably isn't like Deadpool, it's probably something a lot more violent. Like the flesh around the stump expands and bulges, stretching as bones are forced to grow and push out. A big throbbing, agonizing mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-14-2016, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:44:22-07:00","id":890955,"title":"","content":"I assume you mean werewolf. Yes, the arm will grow back. Yes, if you pick it us and hold it in place soon enough it will reattach. Pages 92-93 WtF 2e. <br /> <br /> Uratha regeneration is pretty amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T21:41:36-07:00","id":890985,"title":"","content":"The rules for regeneration clearly state that when the damage the werewolf takes is healed, the tilts associated with these injuries are removed.<br /> <br /> Arm loss is a tilt, a variation of Arm Wrack caused by aggravated damage. Ergo, by recovering all of the aggravated damage that resulted in a lost arm, the werewolf does indeed recover from the lost arm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T23:36:11-07:00","id":891012,"title":"","content":"Hu, so werewolves could literally sell their limbs to other supernatural (ex:goblin market) with no (read: minimal) inconvenience compared to other beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T01:03:34-07:00","id":891032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891012#post891012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hu, so werewolves could literally sell their limbs to other supernatural (ex:goblin market) with no (read: minimal) inconvenience compared to other beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god!! Yes, yes I guess they can. Also: thanks for that horrifyingly disturbing idea that I will definitely use at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T01:41:01-07:00","id":891041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891032#post891032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh god!! Yes, yes I guess they can. Also: thanks for that horrifyingly disturbing idea that I will definitely use at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now if you ever run players through this I have one thing to add. First get them use to trading body parts for boons. Probably by offering great deals for these rare items. After all 'the main hand of a werewolf willingly given' will likely fetch a high price. Then once they are use to selling off things they can just grow back through carefully worded agreement have them sell off their healing factor! How to word it right will be tricky but worth it if you can sneak it past them.<br /> <br /> Because after all if a werewolf can regrow whole missing limbs what horror it would be to have even minor wounds last upon their body!<br /> (Of course this is either temporary or you give opportunity to retrieve their lost 'vitality')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T01:53:35-07:00","id":891044,"title":"","content":"Yes, indeed, they could. Now, I think only foolish or maybe inexperienced werewolves (is there such a thing as a &quot;naive&quot; werewolf?) would do this, of course. You're giving away a piece of yourself to unknown beings with unknown powers. That pretty much spells &quot;disaster waiting to happen&quot; about as much as can be. Needless to say, I think most werewolves would <i>probably </i>shun the idea of selling severed body parts, both because it could easily violate the Oath and for more practical reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T02:21:36-07:00","id":891052,"title":"","content":"The idea would not be one a common wolf would agree to. Rather a single foolish or desperate wolf tempted with promises that'd solve their plight. Maybe it is a piece of knowledge they need to defeat an idiam. Then after an act of desperation the wolf agrees &quot;An eye for an eye&quot; and sells a single eye for the secret weakness of an idiiam. This secret pans out and truly was what the werewolf bartered for. Next time they are searching for some lost scrap of knowledge or fabled bane they can't help but wonder if the merchant might have it as they hit dead end after dead end with a deadline looming. Lo and behold even if he does not have it on him he can fetch it for a price and though the price is high just as it was before it is a fair enough trade. After a time what was once an act out of desperation could be a willing choice. He had never cheated you yet so you trust him. Everything he ever sold you was always as advertised so you trust him. He never asks for more than you can live without for a time so you trust him.<br /> <br /> Just once would a single merchant need to convince a wolf that it was worth it. Just once would one have to offer solution for flesh before hooking the desperate or the foolish. After all if your eyes regrew in less than a week could you put up with being blind temporarily if it saves your pack? Of course you would and that is exactly what the merchant hopes. The first time for noblest of causes. The second because it worked before and other options are drying up. Until they come and sell bit and pieces for trifles and trinkets to solve their every whim and trouble.<br /> <br /> This is meant to spell 'disaster waiting to happen' but because it worked last time the foolish or the desperate come to trust the man that wants to buy them piece by piece... when one can regrow limbs you have to slip mental horror into your physical horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:12:54-07:00","id":891060,"title":"","content":"Realization in direct response to OP: as long as it wasn't caused by silver or supernatural means you could possibly regrow an arm in half an hour. Even 'massive body devistation' is downgraded to Lethal so with just a bit of essance you can heal even faster and your injury won't even impact you more than the pain it caused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:43:01-07:00","id":891069,"title":"","content":"This story is true. Once there was a young werewolf, a pup, called Red-Path, because he left a trail of blood and bodies behind him. He was a warrior, and a good one, no doubt. Skilled as any pit fighter you'll ever see and twice as mean. Red-Path loved only one thing more than the heat and blood of battle: his wife. Red-Path never left her, you see, not like he should have. He kept her at arm's length, tried to do right by her, but the bloodlust, the hunt, it called him. Sooner or later, our most loved ones end up in the crossfire. Usually, that means your pack, pup. They can handle themselves. We're born to this life. It's harsh, definitely, but your pack-sister can take the punishment better than your wife, or mother, or daughter. Some of us try to hold one to what we knew. In Red-Path's case, it might have been the only thing keeping him from becoming a really ravenous monster.<br /> <br /> It wasn't to be. A fighter like Red, he makes lots of enemies. And one day this Azlu, a real nasty piece of work that Red's pack had just torn to shreds along with her nest, followed him home. Yeah, you can see where I'm going with this. It ... wasn't pretty. Red-Path goes off on a hunt, chasing down the other Azlu, but it was all a distraction by this fuckin' <i>mean </i>crone he'd gone and pissed off. And while Red-Path is away, she takes his old lady, right, and \u2014 no, no, not that way. At least if she'd eaten the poor woman's brain it would have been over quick. No, she starts by terrorizing the poor human, then she bites her, see, and puts her in a coma. She merges with her in that really fucking <i>unholy </i>way they do, and then she spins this big web over everything Red-Path cherishes and waits. Just waits. He comes home to check on his old lady, gets caught in the webs, and down she comes, wearing the face of his wife on the spider's bloated body. Well, Red-Path goes berserk, as you might expect, and they rip each other to shreds. She wanted to take everything from him, the spinner crone did, but she hadn't counted on just how <i>angry </i>he'd get. Red-Path killed her, without his pack. And he kept ripping at the pieces until all the floorboards were soaked in so much blood you couldn't tell whose it was: his, the Azlu's, his wife's, what. Just blood, fur, shards of spider armor everywhere. The whole house came down. He had nothin' left.<br /> <br /> Red-Path didn't have much lucidity left in him after that. But what he did have he used to try to get her back. Now normally we mourn, we sing our wolf-dirge, we maybe hunt down the <i>shartha </i>for some good old-fashioned tooth-and-claw revenge. Not Red-Path. He'd been wounded, but it wasn't venom or spider-fangs that got him deepest. And he wasn't about to let go. Not yet. So he had heard of these real strange things, right, these ... these <i>fae</i>, like the ones that dance in the faerie rings and finish an old man's shoes for him, that kind of shit. 'Course, they're real dark, just like a lot of the old tales. Not this cartoon movie crap, but I mean the kinds of things you don't bargain with unless you know what you're doin' \u2014 and if you know what you're doin', you don't bargain with them. It's just askin' for trouble. But old Red-Path is fearless. So he goes to this sort of market they have, with goblins and trinkets and fuckin' straw-men and house-gulping tornadoes and everything else you could imagine. Every fairy tale come to life right there. Most of us just stay away from that shit. Spirits, hell <i>people</i> are weird enough without adding in even <i>weirder</i> things that we know <i>less</i> about.<br /> <br /> Red-Path goes to this market and he looks for someone who can grant him a wish. Anyone or anything that can bring back his beloved. Of course, he offers up any price in return, which is where he went wrong. Damn right he found a taker. Some old goblin or something, I don't know, who wanted a piece of him for every piece of her restored. So he gives up an arm. Naturally, he grows it back. He gives up a leg. His eye. Then the other. Then it gets down to the fuckin' nitty-gritty: teeth, hair, nails. But at last his patron has rebuilt his wife from all these pieces. She's not yet human, though, right? Not aware. Like a zombie, or some kind of soulless shell. She needs a <i>heart</i>, to live again. To be human. He realizes he can't give that without risking death, but he has this brilliant idea. No price is too high, right? So he rips out his own heart there on the spot. Now, normally, even we would have trouble with that. You might survive, if you're quick enough on the mend, but it's risky. So Red-Path takes on Gauru form to heal up faster. Seems like a good idea, right?<br /> <br /> Problem is, it worked. All of it. She gets his heart, and she comes to life right there in the market. Unfortunately, she sees this (literally!) heartless monster standing before her where her husband was, so what does she do? She runs screaming in terror. And Red-Path, overcome with all this rage and now without a heart, without any mercy, gives in to the instinct to chase. He comes to with his heart regenerated but covered in his wife's blood, having killed her a second time with his own claws. Yeah, I know. Fuckin' <i>tragic</i>, is what it is. So anyway, the story goes that Red-Path ripped out his own heart again right there and gave it to the goblin vendor, and let himself bleed out and die.<br /> <br /> But somewhere, in a market full of impossible oddities and broken dreams, there's a jar with a heart in it. The heart still beats to this day. And that, pup, is why we <i>don't sell our fucking body parts to creatures of the night.</i> Remember Red-Path's tale, young one, and remember that sometimes it's best to just let go of something, lest you rip out your own heart trying to keep it close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:51:40-07:00","id":891071,"title":"","content":"Good one Claire <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:53:28-07:00","id":891073,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, esteemed sir! It just sparked in inspiration after thinking about the subject for a few and I wrote it on the spot, making it up as I go. Gotta love that spontaneous creative urge!<br /> <br /> Great work on The Pack, by the way. Loving it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T04:08:52-07:00","id":891080,"title":"","content":"God daaaaamn, that's amazing!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T05:11:07-07:00","id":891091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891073#post891073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much, esteemed sir! It just sparked in inspiration after thinking about the subject for a few and I wrote it on the spot, making it up as I go. Gotta love that spontaneous creative urge!</div> </div> </div> </div>I do love when inspiration strikes like that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891073#post891073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great work on The Pack, by the way. Loving it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T05:17:10-07:00","id":891093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=890953#post890953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limbs can grow back, I imagine it similar to Deadpool's hand. But more painful, since regeneration hurts. So if they had some time and skill, as well as the necessary pieces, a werewolf would probably sew it back on and as a Storyteller I'd rule that it would take less time to heal.<br /> <br /> On second thought after re-reading the section it probably isn't like Deadpool, it's probably something a lot more violent. Like the flesh around the stump expands and bulges, stretching as bones are forced to grow and push out. A big throbbing, agonizing mess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But at least it's mercifully quick. Don't they regenerate to full health instantly unless the damage is caused by silver or some other supernatural weakness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T05:44:16-07:00","id":891100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891093#post891093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at least it's mercifully quick. Don't they regenerate to full health instantly unless the damage is caused by silver or some other supernatural weakness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in Gauru do the regenerate all bashing and lethal every turn. Otherwise it's (at least) one bashing per turn and one lethal every 15 minutes. (Essence expenditure can speed this along.)<br /> <br /> Aggravated damage, such as through limb loss, is one per four days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T05:52:01-07:00","id":891103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891100#post891100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only in Gauru do the regenerate all bashing and lethal every turn. Otherwise it's (at least) one bashing per turn and one lethal every 15 minutes. (Essence expenditure can speed this along.)<br /> <br /> Aggravated damage, such as through limb loss, is one per four days.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ouchies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still if I met something violent enough to take off body parts, I would expect to break out Gauru form the second there were no witnesses around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T06:21:22-07:00","id":891111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891103#post891103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ouchies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still if I met something violent enough to take off body parts, I would expect to break out Gauru form the second there were no witnesses around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but it doesn't help with aggravated damage, if someone can hurt you enough to make aggravated stick!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T07:32:06-07:00","id":891140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891060#post891060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realization in direct response to OP: as long as it wasn't caused by silver or supernatural means you could possibly regrow an arm in half an hour. Even 'massive body devistation' is downgraded to Lethal so with just a bit of essance you can heal even faster and your injury won't even impact you more than the pain it caused.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is wrong. You can't lop an arm off without doing aggravated. It's just not possible. What this mean is that stuff that would be enough to severe a normal person's arm will fail to do so on a werewolf unless it inflict enough damage to wrap around into aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T08:31:03-07:00","id":891160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891140#post891140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is wrong. You can't lop an arm off without doing aggravated. It's just not possible. What this mean is that stuff that would be enough to severe a normal person's arm will fail to do so on a werewolf unless it inflict enough damage to wrap around into aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Story teller used.. ( this is out of my element sorry. Vamps are my thing ) A slasher? where if they do 5L off goes a limb as part of their ability. As wolves are immune to stuff that does Aggravated we thought it might not work,but It says only 5L and it's off.. So that's not aggravated. Anyway. That's what sparked this. Thanks for all your help with this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T09:28:42-07:00","id":891196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891012#post891012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hu, so werewolves could literally sell their limbs to other supernatural (ex:goblin market) with no (read: minimal) inconvenience compared to other beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt I'd let them off so easily in my games. When I'm running a goblin market, what is paid is inevitably gone. If someone buys something for a song, yeah, they need to sing it, but they will also never be able to hear it again. Instead, whenever the song plays, they will hear gibberish if anything. In the case of the werewolf that seeks to sell a hand, in my games the poor bastard would find that, while the wounds may heal, the hand doesn't grow back. If he wants to get the use of that limb back, though, there's another vendor that would gladly sell him a brand new hand. Of course, that will cost him an arm and a leg. Luckily for him, it doesn't necessarily need to be <i>his</i> arm or leg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T09:34:22-07:00","id":891200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891140#post891140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is wrong. You can't lop an arm off without doing aggravated. It's just not possible. What this mean is that stuff that would be enough to severe a normal person's arm will fail to do so on a werewolf unless it inflict enough damage to wrap around into aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough the exception comes from Werewolf itself, specifically the Crimson Falx fetish. 'Effect: After activation, the first enemy struck with the Falx in a scene suffers the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Tilt (attacker's choice) permanently, as the weapon chops the limb clean off.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T09:43:14-07:00","id":891203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891200#post891200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interestingly enough the exception comes from Werewolf itself, specifically the Crimson Falx fetish. 'Effect: After activation, the first enemy struck with the Falx in a scene suffers the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Tilt (attacker's choice) permanently, as the weapon chops the limb clean off.'</div> </div> </div> </div>These secondary effects of Weapons/Maneuvers are indeed a bit confusing, as they contradict the base rules. As a fix for this, we usually upgrade a level of Lethal to Aggravated damage on the attack, to explain the severed limb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T09:45:42-07:00","id":891206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891196#post891196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt I'd let them off so easily in my games. When I'm running a goblin market, what is paid is inevitably gone. If someone buys something for a song, yeah, they need to sing it, but they will also never be able to hear it again. Instead, whenever the song plays, they will hear gibberish if anything. In the case of the werewolf that seeks to sell a hand, in my games the poor bastard would find that, while the wounds may heal, the hand doesn't grow back. If he wants to get the use of that limb back, though, there's another vendor that would gladly sell him a brand new hand. Of course, that will cost him an arm and a leg. Luckily for him, it doesn't necessarily need to be <i>his</i> arm or leg.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't remove the healing factor that way, I would go for something like that. Maybe the hand grows back with a life of its own or some really nasty condition that really adds to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T09:45:52-07:00","id":891207,"title":"","content":"I would just have it do Lethal, then add the limb dropping off from that damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:28:39-07:00","id":891226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891140#post891140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is wrong. You can't lop an arm off without doing aggravated. It's just not possible. What this mean is that stuff that would be enough to severe a normal person's arm will fail to do so on a werewolf unless it inflict enough damage to wrap around into aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't aggravated classified as supernatural damage?<br /> <br /> Hacking off a limb is pretty easy with a blade. Take machetes for example!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:31:32-07:00","id":891229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891196#post891196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he wants to get the use of that limb back, though, there's another vendor that would gladly sell him a brand new hand. Of course, that will cost him an arm and a leg. Luckily for him, it doesn't necessarily need to be <i>his</i> arm or leg.</div> </div> </div> </div>A whole arm and leg for just one hand? Sounds like the Goblin's a cheap ass!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:01:10-07:00","id":891251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891226#post891226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't aggravated classified as supernatural damage?<br /> <br /> Hacking off a limb is pretty easy with a blade. Take machetes for example!</div> </div> </div> </div>No supernatural damage can be bashing, lethal or aggravated. Just like non supernatural damage. For humans some damage is straight up aggravated. Werewolf only take lethal from those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:07:15-07:00","id":891257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891044#post891044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, indeed, they could. Now, I think only foolish or maybe inexperienced werewolves (is there such a thing as a &quot;naive&quot; werewolf?) would do this, of course. You're giving away a piece of yourself to unknown beings with unknown powers. That pretty much spells &quot;disaster waiting to happen&quot; about as much as can be. Needless to say, I think most werewolves would <i>probably </i>shun the idea of selling severed body parts, both because it could easily violate the Oath and for more practical reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't even need to be arcane mindful to realize, that you can be easily tracked from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:11:19-07:00","id":891262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891257#post891257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't even need to be arcane mindful to realize, that you can be easily tracked from it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, every werewolf is capable of tracking you just with some blood they tasted. They'd be well aware of such danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:55:54-07:00","id":891292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891140#post891140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is wrong. You can't lop an arm off without doing aggravated. It's just not possible. What this mean is that stuff that would be enough to severe a normal person's arm will fail to do so on a werewolf unless it inflict enough damage to wrap around into aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal damage to Uratha&quot;<br /> <br /> Would you not say that an arm being cut off falls under 'massive bodily devistation'? The only sources of aggrivated damage for a werewolf are silver or supernatural. So if they can only lose a limb as you say because of aggrivated damage then a chainsaw couldn't take their arm off. Where by my reading of the above it could but the werewolf could regrow it in a turn or two for some essance. If losing your arm doesn't count as massive bodily devistation I don't know what would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:54:23-07:00","id":891352,"title":"","content":"You have to understand it as follow. They can take direct aggravated damage from a source other than supernatural or silver. But they still upgrade lethal into aggravated if they fill their health track.<br /> <br /> Combine that with the tilt that specify a limb is only chopped off if you take aggravated damage and you end up in a situation where a werewolf only lose a limb if an attack deal enough lethal damage to upgrade all the way into lethal.<br /> <br /> It's a rather moot point however because, as far as I'm aware, there is no actual source of damage that deal non supernatural aggravated damage. No exemple is given in the book. It's really up to the storyteller to say &quot;alright, this deal 2 aggravated damage to you&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:01:51-07:00","id":891357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891352#post891352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a rather moot point however because, as far as I'm aware, there is no actual source of damage that deal non supernatural aggravated damage. No exemple is given in the book. It's really up to the storyteller to say &quot;alright, this deal 2 aggravated damage to you&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Weapons fifth dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:05:13-07:00","id":891361,"title":"","content":"Poor example on my part I do admit.<br /> <br /> Edit: though on reflecting on your points <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2547\" data-vbnamecard=\"2547\">Elderand</a> I must admit you do have valid points. Any rebuttals I could come up with I feel don't hold any water. So I'll admit that since it'd require a full track of lethal to cause the aggravated that aggravated would not be downgraded unless it was caused by someone with the 5th dot of heavy weapons as Ephsy pointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 05-15-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:46:12-07:00","id":891934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891206#post891206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I wouldn't remove the healing factor that way, I would go for something like that. Maybe the hand grows back with a life of its own or some really nasty condition that really adds to the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be more likely to do something like that with a strange replacement limb that was purchased. Of course, a werewolf that wished to sell himself at the goblin market without losing the loss of his hand could always cut it off, then regrow it in advance. That would get around the permanent loss of it, as there is a big difference between &quot;this hand in the jar&quot; and &quot;my hand&quot;. If the werewolf offers &quot;my hand,&quot; though, then it is just gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891229#post891229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A whole arm and leg for just one hand? Sounds like the Goblin's a cheap ass!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Well, if you don't want it, that's none of my business. I'm cutting you quite the deal, though. See that guy over there? He's coming for this hand right now. He said he'd be back for it, and there he is! Are you sure you don't want it? Last chance...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T19:23:31-07:00","id":934243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/890951-severed-limbs?p=891012#post891012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hu, so werewolves could literally sell their limbs to other supernatural (ex:goblin market) with no (read: minimal) inconvenience compared to other beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would call letting weird fairy creatures have a piece of yourself to cast who-knows-what magic on you from afar a situation of potentially maximal inconvenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}